Z||000000||Tina||03-15-2001||08:59 PM||||Just ordered the kit, and was wondering<BR>who else has it.<BR>How does it rate on the pothole-scale ?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tina.gif"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||bHooper||03-15-2001||09:53 PM||||i's gots it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>also have poly bushings.<P>and a second rate algnment (read... bad) and cheap tires.<P>i do enjoy it, though.  the car handles and has the potential to do so many things, that it couldnt b4.  <P>just make sure that you have some <B>good</B> rubber on the car, so you can fully enjoy it!<P>i just ran out of $ for what i wanted to do.  i still need to change the front sway bar, and frame bushings+tires.  thats about $600-700 for what i want, though.<P>good luck!<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||6
Z||000002||stimpy||03-15-2001||11:49 PM||||My dad had that set-up on his 86 GT. Pothole scale? I'd invest in a mouthpiece and a kidney belt.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> It ran extremely stiff. Cornered great, but ain't gonna ride like a Cadillac, for sure!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||03-16-2001||12:09 AM||||I have the same on my car. Yes it is STIFF, But I love how it handles! I think it looks great lowered also. If you plan on using it for a daily driver in a pot-holed area, Buy a kidney belt and extra foam cushions. To give an example of how stiff it really is, Before I changed the suspension the rear of the Fiero would lower .7 inches if I sat on the lip of the trunk. After the swap my Fiero it dropped .3 inches. So the suspension is more than double the stiffness of a stock V-6 Fiero.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Hartz||03-16-2001||06:49 PM||||I've got that set up with some crappy Goodyear Eagles.  Handles like a slot car and rides like a dump truck.  I love it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Hartz<BR>'85 SE V6 Turbo<BR>and new (to me) '84 SC V8||||reg||12
